{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And YHWH from Zion roars</b> — a great thunder, like <i>the sound of Your thunder in the whirlwind</i> (Psalms 29:9?) in the manner of <i>and YHWH made the camp of Aram hear</i> (2 Kings 7:6), and thus it is written: <i>YHWH gave ambushes</i> (2 Kings 7:6)." "<b>And they tremble</b> — by way of parable, for all will fear. And HaShem will give strength to His people, in the manner of <i>YHWH will give strength to His people</i> (Psalms 29:11), as I have explained it." "<b>And the meaning of \"from Zion\"</b> — it is that which he [Joel] explained."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "First proof text cited only by opening words; full clause in 2 Kings 7:6. The Psalms reference is reconstructed from context as the phrase 'קול רעמך בגלגל' which does not correspond exactly to any standard verse; possibly corrupt or paraphrased.", 1 "Verse reference for the quoted phrase is Psalms 29:11; not given explicitly in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:50.821986700Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}